WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.709
Close the browser.

00:00:01.989 --> 00:00:03.013
Come back later.

00:00:03.293 --> 00:00:04.531
The work is still here.

00:00:04.811 --> 00:00:08.667
Scheme puts the terminals on your computer
within reach of the screen in front

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:09.013
of you.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.243
Your projects live on the host.

00:00:16.523 --> 00:00:17.974
Your tools run there too.

00:00:18.254 --> 00:00:22.411
Another desktop, a laptop, or a smaller
screen becomes a window into that

00:00:22.411 --> 00:00:24.803
workspace through your private connection.

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.323
The viewing device only needs a browser.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.901
Start with a plain Shell.

00:00:33.181 --> 00:00:36.275
Choose a project folder, name the session,
and get to work.

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:40.075
Keep your launch checks in one tab and
your next idea in another.

00:00:40.355 --> 00:00:43.128
Here, a real example project runs its
tests.

00:00:43.408 --> 00:00:45.392
Switch tasks without losing your place.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.373
When the tabs multiply, search the session
overview.

00:00:55.653 --> 00:00:57.744
Find a familiar name or project.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:02.397
Supported tools can also supply request
excerpts and observed actions.

00:01:02.677 --> 00:01:06.953
The useful details stay beside the
session, so getting back to work takes
less

00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:07.392
hunting.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.803
Use Shell on its own, or choose Claude
Code, Codex, or a local model when

00:01:13.803 --> 00:01:14.379
installed.

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:17.965
Your own accounts, sign-ins, and hardware
power those tools.

00:01:18.245 --> 00:01:20.229
Scheme brings the terminals together.

00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:24.983
The local option checks its endpoint and
model first, and does not silently

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.355
fall back to the cloud.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.163
Keep supported activity, project state,
model information, and usage close to

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:38.933
the terminal.

00:01:39.213 --> 00:01:43.224
These are observations from your tools,
and some may be missing or delayed.

00:01:43.504 --> 00:01:44.912
Unknown stays unknown.

00:01:45.192 --> 00:01:48.349
It does not mean idle, zero usage, or
spare quota.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.200
Have a screenshot to work from?

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.357
Attach it to the current project.

00:01:55.637 --> 00:01:59.605
Scheme stores the upload on your host,
where your terminal tools can use it.

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:02.936
Review the file and its destination before
uploading.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.501
Choose light, dark, or the device's own
preference.

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:15.325
Keep the side panel open for context, or
hide it for more terminal space.

00:02:15.605 --> 00:02:18.656
The terminal stays dark so its colors
remain readable.

00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:24.224
The Connect view explains how to reach
your host from another device.

00:02:24.504 --> 00:02:29.659
This demonstration uses an actual private
S S H tunnel between two desktop

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:30.286
machines.

00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:34.534
A private Tailscale route is also
documented for remote access.

00:02:34.814 --> 00:02:38.419
Scheme runs on your computer; the public
website is the guide.

00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:45.859
Closing the browser detaches the screen.

00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:47.526
The host can keep working.

00:02:47.806 --> 00:02:52.427
In this Linux demonstration, restarting
Scheme's web service also leaves the

00:02:52.427 --> 00:02:55.102
same terminal running, and its job
finishes.

00:02:55.382 --> 00:02:56.576
Keep the host awake.

00:02:56.856 --> 00:03:01.173
A reboot ends running processes, even when
saved tabs or supported

00:03:01.173 --> 00:03:02.808
conversations can reopen.

00:03:09.683 --> 00:03:14.529
On a smaller touch screen, Read turns
recent terminal output into a readable

00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:15.102
snapshot.

00:03:15.382 --> 00:03:19.371
Enlarge the text, change wrapping, copy
it, or request more history.

00:03:19.651 --> 00:03:21.635
Refresh when you want a new snapshot.

00:03:21.915 --> 00:03:26.203
This is the real responsive interface
shown in browser touch emulation.

00:03:31.683 --> 00:03:33.646
Write gives each session its own draft.

00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:36.443
Compose the thought before it reaches the
terminal.

00:03:36.723 --> 00:03:39.198
Insert only lets you inspect the text
first.

00:03:39.478 --> 00:03:41.014
Send and Enter submits it.

00:03:41.294 --> 00:03:44.878
Here, both actions are demonstrated with a
harmless Shell command.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:49.318
Drafts are temporary browser storage, so
save important work properly.

00:03:56.683 --> 00:03:59.243
The touch key bar keeps terminal keys
nearby.

00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:02.446
Open Tools for text size, theme, and
Focus.

00:04:02.726 --> 00:04:05.520
The same workspace adapts to the available
screen.

00:04:08.683 --> 00:04:09.985
One place for the work.

00:04:10.265 --> 00:04:11.950
More freedom in how you reach it.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.982
Scheme is free, open source, and self-
hosted.

00:04:15.262 --> 00:04:19.192
Explore the capabilities, watch the setup
walkthrough, and start with your

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.254
first Shell session.
